// W4e surface fold-in — shell double-quoted strings (parse-only fixture).
//
// GRADUATION: the shell DSL's double-quoted string enters the PBG grammar now
// (wyrd-83wx) as ONE string atom — a `"`-delimited run of fragment text (with
// interior spaces preserved), `\.` escapes, and `$name` / `${name}` parameter
// expansions — rather than the juxtaposed shell words it previously degraded
// to. The labeler's shell double-quote mode lexes the constituent tokens, and
// `double_quoted_string` is rewired off its dead `variable_expansion` /
// `command_substitution` composite tiles onto the inline expansion shape
// (command substitution inside a string is the deferred POSIX tail). The
// SEMANTICS (field-splitting-free expansion into a single argument) graduate
// under the wyrd-83wx gandr-shell wiring follow-up. Parse-only; never lowered.

// A quoted argument with interior spaces is ONE word, not two.
#!{ echo "hello world"; }

// Escapes are live inside double quotes (a tab and a newline).
#!{ printf "col1\tcol2\n"; }

// Parameter expansion inside double quotes: simple and braced, interleaved
// with literal fragments.
#!{ echo "home is $HOME and user is ${USER}"; }

// Single- and double-quoted arguments side by side: the single-quoted run is
// verbatim (its `$x` stays literal), the double-quoted run expands.
#!{ printf '%s\n' "value $x"; }
